			"output": {
				"text": "1. **Set gates and rehearse.** Baseline peak-hour p99 latency, error rate, throughput, and database saturation. Set numeric promotion and rollback thresholds, a breach duration, and a maximum replication lag. Treat any confirmed critical data mismatch as an immediate stop. Assign a cutover owner and rehearse both cutover and rollback under peak load.\n\n2. **Backfill while the source owns writes.** Take a consistent snapshot, record its change-log position, and copy in throttled batches. Replay changes from that position, including deletes, in commit order with idempotent retries. Pause the backfill if source health degrades. **Gate:** at a common checkpoint, partition checksums and business invariants match, and replication lag stays within budget under peak traffic.\n\n3. **Shadow reads.** Mirror a sample of production reads to the target without serving its responses. Compare results at equivalent data versions so replication lag is not mistaken for corruption. Dashboard latency, errors, saturation, lag, and mismatches by endpoint and database. **Gate:** no unexplained differences; target performance meets the agreed thresholds.\n\n4. **Canary served reads.** Route stable cohorts to the target in steps, for example 1% \u2192 5% \u2192 25% \u2192 100%. Keep read-after-write requests on the source unless the target has applied the required commit. Promote only after a representative observation window at each step, including peak load before full rollout. **Rollback:** return reads to the source on a threshold breach or critical mismatch.\n\n5. **Switch write ownership.** Briefly queue new writes, drain in-flight source writes, fence the source writer, and verify the target has applied the final source commit. Enable target writes and release the queue. Start reverse replication from the cutover checkpoint, with only the target accepting application writes. **Rollback:** fence target writes, drain and verify reverse replication through the last acknowledged commit, then reopen the source. If catch-up cannot be verified, hold writes rather than fail back to stale data.\n\n6. **Soak and retire.** Keep the source synchronized through the agreed rollback window. **Exit gate:** peak-load SLOs hold, reconciliation remains clean, and a target backup has been successfully restored. Only then stop reverse replication and retire the source."
			},
