				"text": "```ts\nasync function withRetry<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  initialDelayMs = 100,\n): Promise<T> {\n  const maxRetries = 3;\n\n  for (let attempt = 0; ; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (attempt >= maxRetries) throw error;\n\n      const delayMs = initialDelayMs * 2 ** attempt;\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, delayMs));\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe first attempt runs immediately. If it fails, the helper retries up to three times, waiting 100 ms, 200 ms, then 400 ms by default. If all four attempts fail, it rethrows the last error.\n\n```ts\nconst status = await withRetry(async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://example.com/status\");\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n  return response.text();\n});\n\nconsole.log(status);\n```"
